From 339da65a4c401141bc488f1be6302af6fa2aad71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrija Panic <andrija.panic@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:08:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add UEFI bootloader fix rule for Debian 13

Debian 13 uses the same shim-based EFI layout as Debian 11 and 12
(/boot/efi/EFI/debian/{shim,grub}<arch>.efi and grub.cfg) but was
missing from the UEFI fix pattern match, so converting a UEFI Debian 13
guest logs "No UEFI fix rule for debian 13" and "Can't fix UEFI
bootloader. VM may not boot". The converted VM then stops in the
firmware with no bootable option: the new NVRAM has no entry for
\EFI\debian\shimx64.efi and Debian's installer does not create the
fallback loader at \EFI\BOOT\BOOTX64.EFI by default.

Observed with virt-v2v-in-place 2.7.1 (el9) converting a Debian 13.4
guest from vSphere 8.0.3 to qcow2 on KVM. Starting the guest once from
the UEFI shell (FS0:\EFI\debian\shimx64.efi) and running
grub-install --force-extra-removable inside it, which creates the same
fallback loader this rule creates, made it boot unattended.

Signed-off-by: Andrija Panic <andrija.panic@gmail.com>

Backport to virt-v2v 2.7.1 (rhel-9.8) of upstream commit
bf4e7e1874cfb2c4e17bacb6c28ae8ac597cfb8a, pull request
https://github.com/libguestfs/virt-v2v/pull/201, released in
virt-v2v 2.13.8.  Applied without conflicts.

(cherry picked from commit bf4e7e1874cfb2c4e17bacb6c28ae8ac597cfb8a)
---
 convert/convert_linux.ml | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/convert/convert_linux.ml b/convert/convert_linux.ml
index 31d249b8..e5833563 100644
--- a/convert/convert_linux.ml
+++ b/convert/convert_linux.ml
@@ -1390,7 +1390,8 @@ let convert (g : G.guestfs) source inspect i_firmware _ keep_serial_console _ =
                   g inspect.i_root "fix uefi boot" fix_script)
               else
                 cant_fix_uefi ()
-            | ("ubuntu", 14) | ("debian", 11) | ("debian", 12) ->
+            | ("ubuntu", 14) | ("debian", 11) | ("debian", 12)
+            | ("debian", 13) ->
               (* to make a bootable uefi ubuntu 14 we need to
                * copy shim<arch>.efi to UEFI fallback path
                * and rename it to BOOT<arch>.efi, also we copy
